VALUES ('SBAC','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for wireless communications towers, site leasing, development, tenant amendments, and long-term infrastructure contracts can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Vacancy, churn, customer consolidation, or property obsolescence can reduce cash flow. Leverage and maturities expose owners to rates and capital-market availability. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','SBAC SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001034054&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides SBA COMMUNICATIONS REIT CORP CLASS''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
