VALUES ('SMCI','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for server and storage systems, AI infrastructure, rack-scale integration, liquid cooling, motherboard design, and data-center deployment can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Products can lose relevance as architectures, standards, or customer preferences change. Large customers, distributors, foundries, or partners can alter demand and bargaining power. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','SMCI SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001375365&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides SUPER MICRO COMPUTER INC''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
