VALUES ('SPCX','bull_case','editorial_analysis','Connectivity generated $11.387 billion of 2025 revenue, $4.423 billion of operating income, and $7.168 billion of Segment Adjusted EBITDA as Starlink subscriptions and enterprise adoption expanded. At March 31, 2026, Starlink served about 10.3 million subscribers across 164 countries, territories, and markets using more than 9,600 broadband and mobile satellites. SpaceX completed 170 launches and placed 2,213 metric tons into orbit in 2025; high cadence, reusability, and vertical integration support both external missions and its own constellation economics. The June IPO sold 555.6 million primary shares at $135, substantially increasing financial capacity for Starship, satellite infrastructure, and AI investment.','Preserves the constructive interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','SpaceX official website','https://www.spacex.com/','SpaceX publishes official mission, vehicle, human-spaceflight, Starship, and company information. Company materials should be distinguished from independently verified results and SEC-filed financial statements.','2026-08-01','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
