VALUES ('SPCX','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Consolidated net loss was $4.937 billion in 2025 and $4.276 billion in Q1 2026; strong Connectivity profit did not translate into consolidated GAAP profit. Total 2025 capital expenditures were $20.737 billion versus $6.785 billion of operating cash flow, and Q1 2026 capex accelerated to $10.107 billion. The AI segment generated $3.201 billion of 2025 revenue but a $6.355 billion operating loss and $12.727 billion of capex; management describes a multi-year path before sustained positive segment EBITDA. Elon Musk held approximately 82.4% of post-offering voting power, leaving public Class A owners with very limited influence over governance, board composition, related-party decisions, and capital allocation.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','SpaceX Final IPO Prospectus','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1181412/000162828026042639/spaceexplorationtechnologi.htm','The final prospectus describes SpaceX''s Space, Connectivity, and AI segments; historical financial statements; Starlink and launch metrics; xAI integration; risk factors; capital structure; IPO terms; founder voting control; and use of proceeds.','2026-08-01','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
