VALUES ('SPCX','thesis_breaker','editorial_analysis','The thesis breaks if Starlink subscriber growth and network efficiency cannot outrun falling ARPU and satellite replacement costs while Starship and AI continue consuming capital at returns below SpaceX''s funding cost. Technical achievements alone would not protect owner value if consolidated free cash flow remains structurally negative or governance permits persistent cross-subsidization without measurable returns.','Defines evidence that would invalidate the ownership thesis.','SpaceX Final IPO Prospectus','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1181412/000162828026042639/spaceexplorationtechnologi.htm','The final prospectus describes SpaceX''s Space, Connectivity, and AI segments; historical financial statements; Starlink and launch metrics; xAI integration; risk factors; capital structure; IPO terms; founder voting control; and use of proceeds.','2026-08-01','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
