VALUES ('TSLA','revenue_model','editorial_analysis','Vehicle and energy-product sales, regulatory credits, leasing, paid software and connectivity, services and used vehicles, charging, insurance, energy generation, and project or service contracts. Future mobility and robotics economics depend on utilization, take rate, safety, regulation, hardware life, service cost, and capital ownership.','Explains how reported activity converts into revenue and owner economics.','Tesla Second-Quarter 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000162828026049270/tsla-20260630.htm','The filing reports Q2 and first-half revenue, segment gross profit, net income, cash flow, capital expenditures, liquidity, Robotaxi and AI investment, regulatory credits, legal matters, related-party transactions, and risk disclosures.','2026-07-22','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
