VALUES ('TSLA','owner_requirements','editorial_analysis','Vehicle demand and price realization must support adequate manufacturing returns; Energy must convert deployments into durable gross profit and cash flow; the 2026 capex step-up must earn attractive returns; FSD and Robotaxi must produce measurable paid usage with acceptable safety and regulation; and Optimus must advance from demonstrations to repeatable manufacturing and customer value.','Makes the conditions required by the thesis explicit and testable.','Tesla Second-Quarter 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000162828026049270/tsla-20260630.htm','The filing reports Q2 and first-half revenue, segment gross profit, net income, cash flow, capital expenditures, liquidity, Robotaxi and AI investment, regulatory credits, legal matters, related-party transactions, and risk disclosures.','2026-07-22','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
