VALUES ('TSLA','bull_case','editorial_analysis','Q2 revenue increased 26% to $28.236 billion as automotive, Energy, and services revenue all grew year over year; first-half revenue reached $50.623 billion. Tesla delivered 480,126 vehicles and deployed 13.5 GWh of energy storage in Q2, demonstrating manufacturing and project scale across two large end markets. First-half operating cash flow increased to $8.634 billion, and cash plus short-term investments remained $43.524 billion at June 30, providing unusual capacity to fund new products and infrastructure. FSD subscriptions, Robotaxi operations, charging, services, insurance, and fleet software create multiple paths to increase lifetime revenue per vehicle beyond the original sale.','Preserves the constructive interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','Tesla Q2 2026 Results','https://ir.tesla.com/press-release/tesla-releases-second-quarter-2026-financial-results','Tesla''s official release links the Q2 update, earnings webcast, and investor-relations archive. Company presentation and forward-looking claims should be reconciled to the Form 10-Q.','2026-08-01','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
