VALUES ('TSLA','thesis_breaker','editorial_analysis','The thesis breaks if the vehicle and Energy businesses cannot generate durable cash returns through the investment cycle while autonomy and robotics continue absorbing capital without achieving independently measurable safety, regulatory permission, utilization, and unit economics. A large addressable market would not compensate owners for structurally weak returns on the installed capital base.','Defines evidence that would invalidate the ownership thesis.','Tesla Second-Quarter 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000162828026049270/tsla-20260630.htm','The filing reports Q2 and first-half revenue, segment gross profit, net income, cash flow, capital expenditures, liquidity, Robotaxi and AI investment, regulatory credits, legal matters, related-party transactions, and risk disclosures.','2026-07-22','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
