VALUES ('UBER','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Driver classification and regulation can weaken the owner outcome; monitor laws, minimum pay, benefits, taxes, licenses, and litigation. Competition and incentives can weaken the owner outcome; monitor driver supply, wait times, promotions, take rate, and share. Autonomous disruption can weaken the owner outcome; monitor partnership economics, fleet ownership, routing share, safety, and disintermediation. A valuation that assumes flawless execution can fall even when the underlying business remains viable.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','UBER SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001543151&owner=exclude','Uber Technologies, Inc filings provide the audited financial record, business description, material risks, commitments, governance, and current reports.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
